# Tells fw_printenv/fw_setenv where U-Boot keeps its saved environment.
#
# U-Boot is built here with:
#   CONFIG_ENV_IS_IN_FAT=y
#   CONFIG_ENV_FAT_DEVICE_AND_PART="0:1"
#   CONFIG_ENV_FAT_FILE="uboot.env"
#   CONFIG_ENV_SIZE=0x4000
#
# so the environment is a plain 16 KiB file on the vfat boot partition, not a
# raw offset on a block device. libubootenv accepts a regular file as the
# "device", which is why partition 1 has to be mounted -- see
# var-rootdirs-mnt-bootpart.mount.
#
# The size MUST match CONFIG_ENV_SIZE exactly. If they disagree, fw_setenv
# writes a CRC over the wrong length and U-Boot silently falls back to its
# built-in default environment on the next boot -- which means no OSTree boot
# script, and a device that stops at the U-Boot prompt.
#
# Device            Offset  Size
/mnt/bootpart/uboot.env 0x0000 0x4000
